{#- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The 404 page.

   Two things make this file work, and both are easy to break:

   1. `permalink: /404.html` — a FILE, not a directory. worker.js fetches this
      exact path when the asset lookup misses, so renaming it means unknown
      URLs go back to returning a completely blank body.

   2. `eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true` — without it this page joins the
      collections that feed sitemap.njk, and the site would advertise its own
      error page to search engines as if it were real content.

   No `activePage` is set on purpose: nothing in the nav should light up, since
   the visitor is not on any of those pages.

   Every link below is a real route. Do not add one for a page that does not
   exist yet — a 404 that sends you to another 404 is worse than the blank one
   this replaced.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------- #}
